---
title: "entry_function_validation (Sui Move Concepts: Entry Keyword Rules)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_entry: function marked with entry keyword
    q_check_entry --> q_check_visibility: is entry function
    q_check_entry --> q_skip: not entry function (standard rules apply)
    q_check_visibility --> q_check_return: verify function is private (no public keyword)
    q_check_return --> q_check_return_drop: verify return types have drop ability
    q_check_return_drop --> q_check_inputs: return types all have drop
    q_check_return_drop --> q_abort_return: return type missing drop ability
    q_check_inputs --> q_check_obj_fresh: verify object inputs not used in non-entry functions in same PTB
    q_check_obj_fresh --> q_allow_ptb: object inputs are fresh (not reused)
    q_check_obj_fresh --> q_abort_reuse: object input already used in non-entry function
    q_allow_ptb --> [*]: entry function callable in PTB but not from other packages

    q_skip --> [*]: standard function dispatch
    q_abort_return --> [*]: abort - entry function return type must have drop
    q_abort_reuse --> [*]: abort - entry function object inputs must be fresh in PTB

    note right of q_check_visibility
        INV-001: entry functions should be private (no public keyword)
        INV-002: entry enables PTB calling without exposing to other Move packages
        INV-003: Used for randomness to prevent front-running/back-running
    end note

    note right of q_check_obj_fresh
        INV-004: Object inputs to entry functions cannot be reused from non-entry calls in same PTB
        INV-005: This prevents composability attacks on entry-only functions
    end note
